The details of the assesment simply say the solution has to be related the topic.
Therefore, seeing as interest has two types these should both be implemented to the application.

Simple interest - Interest = principal * interest rate * Time (in years)
Essentially as though you withdrew the interest earnings everytime you were paid rather than putting back into the principal (original amount you started with)


Compound interest - P * (1 + r)^2
                    P Principal
                    r annual interest rate
                    t time (in years)
Accrued funds from interest is added to the original amount and interest applies to that new greater principal.
You are earning interest on interest.


